    {
      "short": "Sticky",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Sticky sessions: always the same server",
      "body": [
        "A quick fix is <span class=\"term\">sticky sessions</span> (session affinity): the balancer sets a cookie recording which server a shopper first used, and keeps sending them there. Priya always reaches server 1, so her cart is always there.",
        "Errors vanish. But stickiness fights the balancer: a server with a few heavy shoppers can't hand them off, and a newly added server only gets <i>new</i> visitors, so it fills up slowly."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "~ Balancer pins each shopper to one server",
        "~ Errors 50% → 0%"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "errors": 0,
        "p95": 150,
        "survive": "no",
        "scale": "limited"
      },
