    {
      "short": "Shared store",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Move the memory out of the server",
      "body": [
        "The real fix: keep sessions in a <span class=\"term\">shared session store</span> — a fast in-memory database such as Redis that every server can reach. The cookie now holds only a session ID; any server can look it up in about a millisecond.",
        "The app servers become <span class=\"term\">stateless</span>: they keep nothing between requests. Any server can handle any request, so the balancer is free to use round robin again."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Shared session store (Redis)",
        "~ Servers keep no session state",
        "- Sticky cookie"
      ],
      "metrics": {
