    {
      "short": "Tokens",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Or let the client carry it",
      "body": [
        "Another option is a <span class=\"term\">signed token</span>, such as a JWT. At login the server signs a small document — “user = Priya, expires 18:00” — and the browser sends it with each request. Any server can verify the signature with a shared key, with no lookup at all.",
        "Tokens suit identity (who you are), less so big or changing data like a cart. And a signed token can't easily be withdrawn: if Priya logs out or is banned, it stays valid until it expires."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Signed token for identity",
        "~ Cart still lives in the store"
      ],
      "metrics": {
